<title>USA: D&amp;P reaffirms IPALCO unit's ratings.</title>
<headline>D&amp;P reaffirms IPALCO unit's ratings.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Monday it reaffirmed the ratings of Indianapolis Power &amp; Light Co following parent company IPALCO Enterprises Inc's announced new financial strategy that includes a dividend cut and recapitalization.</p>
<p>Indianapolis Power's current ratings are as follows: first mortgage bonds and collateralized PCRBs, Double A; non-collateralized PCRBs and preferred stock, Double A Minus; and commercial paper and variable rate mode non-collateralized PCRBs, D One Plus.</p>
<p>	 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
